# Prudent — one .gitignore for a language-neutral root over three tiers.
#
# The root is not a Dart package, so the Flutter patterns below cannot stay anchored at the root
# the way `flutter create` wrote them (`/build/`, `/android/app/debug`). A leading-slash pattern
# matches only at the repository root, so after the client moved into client/ those patterns
# silently stopped matching anything — the ignore file would still look correct and would ignore
# nothing. They are re-anchored to the tier that owns them.

# Miscellaneous
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
.atom/
.build/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
.swiftpm/
migrate_working_dir/

# IntelliJ related
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/

# The .vscode folder contains launch configuration and tasks you configure in
# VS Code which you may wish to be included in version control, so this line
# is commented out by default.
#.vscode/

# --- client/ : Flutter/Dart/Pub ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Unanchored so they match at any depth: the client tier owns them today, and a second Dart
# package (a shared package, a second app) would otherwise need every pattern repeated.
**/doc/api/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
build/

# Symbolication related
app.*.symbols

# Obfuscation related
app.*.map.json

# Android Studio will place build artifacts here
client/android/app/debug
client/android/app/profile
client/android/app/release

# Generated localizations are BUILT, NOT TRACKED (jZen ADR-009): flutter gen-l10n ships inside
# the Flutter SDK every consumer already has, so there is no toolchain boundary to carry the
# output across. Listed now so the first ARB file cannot land with its output tracked by
# accident. Prudent's contract gate asserts none of it is tracked (Phase 1).
client/lib/src/l10n/generated/

# --- server/ : Java/Maven ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# `target/` is unanchored for the same reason as build/: the server is one Maven module today and
# will not stay that way.
target/
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# The staged web (Flutter) and admin (react-admin) bundles `task build:web`/`build:web:admin`
# rsync into META-INF/resources so the native image serves them same-origin (docs/prudent-
# migration-plan.md Phase 5). Staged, never committed: a build artifact baked from a build-time
# API URL has no business in git, and the tracked openapi.yaml one directory up is untouched by
# either task's --delete.
server/src/main/resources/META-INF/resources/
